<title>BELGIUM: BONSAI BONANZA FOR BELGIAN VOLVO PLANT STAFF.</title>
<headline>BONSAI BONANZA FOR BELGIAN VOLVO PLANT STAFF.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volvo's Belgian plant said on Tuesday it was giving personnel 4,000 bonsai trees to reward them for making the plant the first non-Japanese company win the &quot;Total Productive Maintenance&quot; Special Award.</p>
<p>Ghent-based Volvo Cars Europe Industry said in a statement it chose the tiny bonsai trees -- &quot;the result of years of careful pruning and maintenance&quot; -- as a symbol for care and dedication by staff, helping the plant win the quality award.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
